From: RV1106G3 custom board Rev A (design/decisions.md D-93)
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: gpio-poweroff: optional takeover of pm_power_off

OPTIONAL. Apply only if the board log shows
  "gpio-poweroff: gpio_poweroff_probe: pm_power_off function already registered"
(another driver, e.g. PSCI with CONFIG_ARM_PSCI=y, took pm_power_off first).
The board DTS already carries the property "custom,override-pm-power-off";
an unpatched kernel ignores it.

Base: LuckfoxTECH/luckfox-pico sysdrv/source/kernel (Linux 5.10.160)
drivers/power/reset/gpio-poweroff.c (local copy design/refs/luckfox-sdk-boardcfg-2026-10-29/).
---
--- a/drivers/power/reset/gpio-poweroff.c	2026-10-29 09:08:28
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/gpio-poweroff.c	2026-10-29 09:08:28
@@ -51,13 +51,20 @@
 	bool input = false;
 	enum gpiod_flags flags;
 
-	/* If a pm_power_off function has already been added, leave it alone */
-	if (pm_power_off != NULL) {
+	/*
+	 * If a pm_power_off function has already been added, leave it alone,
+	 * unless the board asks for the GPIO to be the power-off method
+	 * (RV1106G3 custom board Rev A: PWR_KILL to the LTC2954 KILL input).
+	 */
+	if (pm_power_off != NULL &&
+	    !device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev, "custom,override-pm-power-off")) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev,
 			"%s: pm_power_off function already registered\n",
 		       __func__);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
+	if (pm_power_off != NULL)
+		dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "replacing the registered pm_power_off handler\n");
 
 	input = device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev, "input");
 	if (input)
